cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BIND in published work, please cite the methods paper
  (see preferred-citation below) as well as the CAMELS and IllustrisTNG
  simulation papers listed in README.md.
title: "BIND: Baryonic INpainting with Deep learning"
abstract: >-
  BIND is a conditional flow-matching emulator that paints baryonic fields
  (dark matter, gas, stars, and optionally four gas-thermodynamic fields)
  onto dark-matter-only halo patches, conditioned on the 35-dimensional
  cosmological and IllustrisTNG galaxy-formation parameter space of the
  CAMELS SB35 suite and, for redshift-conditioned checkpoints, on the
  scale factor. It provides a deployable painting API for arbitrary
  Gadget/Arepo N-body snapshots.
type: software
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Maxelee/BIND"
url: "https://github.com/Maxelee/BIND"
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - baryonic feedback
  - flow matching
  - generative models
  - emulator
  - weak lensing
  - CAMELS
  - IllustrisTNG
